: >object.
: 
: 	Only altars and creatures even have alignments.  The way to determine
: the alignment of an altar or a priest(ess) is with the '/' command.  A co-
: aligned altar or priest(ess) is one which is of the same alignment as your
: character.  A non-co-aligned altar or preist(ess) is one which is not.  There
: are also unaligned altars and priests (two of them) which are unaligned wrt
: any character.

For living creatures, you can also apply a stetheoscope toward it. 
Strangely, it gives you not only the creature's health, but also its
alignment, armor class, and amount of gold being carried.  

If such a device really existed I bet you would see alot of criminals
on the subway here in Chicago carrying it around (hmm, how much money
does this sucker have).  

